          %title Supersymmetry in fractional quantum Hall systems
          %h3#ReferencesSupersymmetryInFractionalQuantumHall Supersymmetry in fractional quantum Hall systems
          %p
            On hidden/emergent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+systems"} fractional quantum Hall systems
            (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Laughlin+wavefunction#SupersymmetryBetweenLaughlinAndMooreReadStates"} SuSy between Laughlin and Moore-Read states
          %blockquote
            %p
              (for a similar phenomenon cf. also
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
          %p
            The density-wave excitations above the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phase+of+matter"} topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+state"} ground state
            of 2D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
            gases in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+systems"} fractional quantum Hall systems
            exhibit an
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesEffectiveFQHSupergeometry"} effective supergeometry
          %p and in the long-wavelength limit are described by an
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesEffectiveFQHSupergravity"}> effective supergravity theory
              \.
          %h4#ReferencesEffectiveFQHSupergeometry Effective FQH Supergeometry
          %p
            The use of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            in the description of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+systems"} fractional quantum Hall systems
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore-Read+state"} Moore-Read state
            is the top
            = succeed "-component" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+field"} super field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laughlin+wavefunction"} Laughlin wavefunction
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Laughlin+wavefunction#SupersymmetryBetweenLaughlinAndMooreReadStates"} there
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuki+Hasebe"}> Kazuki Hasebe
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetric Quantum-Hall Effect on a Fuzzy Supersphere
                %strong 94
                (2005) 206802 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.94.206802"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.94.206802
                ]
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuki+Hasebe"}> Kazuki Hasebe
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Hall liquid on a noncommutative superplane
                %strong 72
                (2005) 105017 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.72.105017"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.72.105017
                ]
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuki+Hasebe"}> Kazuki Hasebe
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Hall Effect Based on SUSY Non-Commutative Geometry
                %strong 171
                (2007) 154–159 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1143/PTPS.171.154"}> doi:10.1143/PTPS.171.154
                ]
            %li#Hasebe08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuki+Hasebe"}> Kazuki Hasebe
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Unification of Laughlin and Moore–Read states in SUSY quantum Hall effect
                %strong 372
                9 (2008) 1516-1520 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physleta.2007.09.071"}> doi:10.1016/j.physleta.2007.09.071
                ]
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuki+Hasebe"}> Kazuki Hasebe
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetric Quantum Hall Liquid with a Deformed Supersymmetry
                %strong 73
                (2010) 345-351 [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.1724"}> arXiv:0901.1724
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1134/S1063778810020225"} doi:10.1134/S1063778810020225
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kazuki+Hasebe"}> Kazuki Hasebe
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetric Quantum Spin Model and Quantum Hall Effect
                %strong 117
                6 (2010) F59- [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.24532/soken.117.6_F59"}> doi:10.24532/soken.117.6_F59
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1687527"} spire:1687527
          %p
            Based on this, the proposal that also the “magnetoroton” and the “neutral fermion” excitations of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo =
                  %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu = 5/2
            Moore&amp;Read-state should be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpartners"} superpartners
            of each other, is due to:
          %ul
            %li#GromovMartinecRyu20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrey+Gromov"}> Andrey Gromov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emil+J.+Martinec"} Emil J. Martinec
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shinsei+Ryu"} Shinsei Ryu
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Collective excitations at filling factor
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 5
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 5/2
              %strong 125
              (2020) 077601 [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.125.077601"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.125.077601
              ,
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.06384"} arXiv:1909.06384
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (via
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
                  formulation)
          %p further discussed in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Ken K. W. Ma, Ruojun Wang, Kun Yang:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Realization of Supersymmetry and Its Spontaneous Breaking in Quantum Hall Edges
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.126.206801"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.126.206801
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.05448"} arXiv:2101.05448
            %li
              %p
                Patricio Salgado-Rebolledo, Giandomenico Palumbo:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nonrelativistic supergeometry in the Moore-Read fractional quantum Hall state
                %strong 106
                (2022) 065020 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.106.065020"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.106.065020
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.14339"} arXiv:2112.14339
            %li{:id => "PuBalramFremlingGromovPapić23"}
              %p
                Songyang Pu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ajit+C.+Balram"} Ajit C. Balram
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrey+Gromov"} Andrey Gromov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Signatures of Supersymmetry in the
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ν
                          %mo =
                          %mn 5
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu = 5/2
                    Fractional Quantum Hall Effect
                %strong 130
                (2023) 176501 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.130.176501"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.130.176501
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.04169"} arXiv:2301.04169
              %blockquote
                %p
                  “Our results suggest that the SUSY structure is intrinsically present in spectral properties of the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ν
                        %mo =
                        %mn 5
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu = 5/2
                  state”
            %li#LiuZhaoXiang24
              %p
                Yang Liu, Tongzhou Zhao, T. Xiang:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Resolving Geometric Excitations of Fractional Quantum Hall States
                %strong 110
                195137 (2024) [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.11195"}> arXiv:2406.11195
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => " https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.110.195137"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.110.195137
              %blockquote
                %p “Our findings support the hypothesis of emergent supersymmetry and highlight the potential for detecting neutral fermions in future experiments.”
            %li
              %p
                Koyena Bose,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ajit+C.+Balram"} Ajit C. Balram
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dispersion of neutral collective modes in partonic fractional quantum Hall states and its applications to paired states of composite fermions
                %strong 112
                3 (2025) [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/p5sq-kczs"}> doi:10.1103/p5sq-kczs
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
